    "repetitionsPerCase": 3,
    "reference": "The same synchronous file policy runs while holding the session mutex. Both modes use the new write helper, so this isolates lock scope rather than comparing historical binaries.",
    "candidate": "Capture immutable audio, metadata, operations and a session-specific save lease; write/backup/rename outside the editor mutex; commit the captured saved anchor to the still-matching session.",
    "workload": "Private synthetic stereo 44.1 kHz float WAV, short gain before each save. First save to an edited version, then update that version with a recoverable backup. Includes real file writes, policy validation, state DTO, filesystem name choice and rename.",
    "limits": [
      "No DB indexing, event delivery, UI, IPC or worker queue delay. No audio device or user library.",
      "Uncontended session and file writer mutexes; does not quantify waiting under real concurrency. Functional concurrency tests cover accessible editor, overlapping saves, competing windows and replaced sessions.",
      "Three local alternating observations, warm filesystem, no cross-platform or p95 guarantee. No fsync/power-failure durability claim.",
      "Phase RSS includes mapped pages and allocator retention, is not peak memory, and excludes WebView.",
      "Disk write time was not reduced consistently. The large first-save median is higher in this candidate observation; the implementation goal here is keeping file I/O out of the editor critical section."
    ]
  },
